Proposed change
---------------
- Extend existing exposed_namespaces() with tracing, profiling and monitoring
  hooks, try/finally boundaries, and implicit/explicit suspension syntax.
- Reject immediate-generator identity proofs involving consumer-name walrus
  writes, multiple/async clauses, explicit producer calls, or unproved eager
  header/generic/class execution contexts.
- Preserve all six existing native consumers, existing namespace/attribute
  safeguards, and the direct native-set-literal add fast path.
- Add 13 source-only frame/helper/consumer boundary cases and four independent
  tracing/monitoring work-limit cases. The eight measured frame cases are
  already maintained by the base commit and are not duplicated here.
- Add an actual module/runner JSON/SARIF case requiring the tracing example's
  LDAP work-limit diagnostic to survive alongside independent analysis errors.

The consumer rule does not prove that arbitrary implicit user protocols are
inert. Broader native identity, constructor-field precision and whole-repository
release qualification remain open.

